# Clean code

Prefer clear names, small focused units, and explicit error handling.

## Required behavior

- Inspect existing project conventions before inventing new ones.
- Prefer readable code over clever abstractions.
- Do not expand scope beyond the requested change.

## Anti-patterns

- Drive-by refactors unrelated to the task.
- Silent catches that hide failures.
